==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rightuous}}, {{l|en|rightwise}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
From earlier {{m|en|rightuous}}, {{m|en|rightwose}}, {{m|en|rightwos}}, {{m|en|rightwise}}, from {{inh|en|enm|rightwise}}, {{m|enm|rightwis}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rihtwīs||righteous, just}}, corresponding to {{suffix|en|right|wise}} (with assimilation of second element to {{m|en|-ous}}), or to {{compound|en|right|wise|t2=way, manner}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|richtwis||righteous}}, {{cog|goh|rehtwīsic||righteous, just}}, {{cog|is|réttvíss||righteous, just}}. Compare also {{l|en|thefteous}}, {{l|en|mighteous}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaɪt͡ʃəs/}}
* {{i|obsolete}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaɪtjəs/|/ˈɹaɪti.əs/}}<ref>{{R:Jespersen MEGoHP|I|12.41|346}}</ref>
* {{audio|en|en-us-righteous.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪtʃəs|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[free|Free]] from [[sin]] or [[guilt]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Proverbs|28|1|passage=The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the '''righteous''' are bolde as a lyon.}}
# [[moral|Moral]] and [[virtuous]], perhaps to the point of [[sanctimony]].
#: {{ux|en|Human beings should take a '''righteous''' path, and so should art. We should promote kindness and beauty through art.}}
# [[justified|Justified]] [[morally]].
#: '''''righteous''' indignation''
# {{lb|en|slang|US}} [[awesome|Awesome]]; [[great]].
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1986|title=Ferris Bueller's Day Off|author=John Hughes|actor=Edie McClurg|role=Grace Wheelberg|medium=Motion Picture|text=The sportos, the motorheads, geeks, sluts, bloods, wastoids, dweebies, dickheads - they all adore him. They think he's a '''righteous''' dude.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1995|author=Norman L. Russell; Doug Grad|title=Suicide Charlie: A Vietnam War Story|page=191
|passage=He sold me a bulging paper sack full of Cambodian Red for two dolla' MPC. A strange experience, copping from a kid, but it was '''righteous''' weed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Stephen King|title=Graduation Afternoon|passage=Tonight the kids will go out and party down in a more '''righteous''' mode. Alcohol and not a few tabs of X will be ingested. Club music will throb through big speakers.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|US}} Major; large; significant.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2021|author=G. S. Jennsen|title=Amaranthe V: Riven
|passage=He found Richard in one piece near a large circular container, thankfully, staring at a '''righteous''' mess of blood and gore.}}

