===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To make righteous; specifically, to [[justify]] religiously, to absolve from sin.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=w:Diarmaid MacCulloch|title=A History of Christianity|page=101|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2010
|passage=Thus for the purposes of being ‘'''righteoused'''’, the Law was irrelevant; yet Paul could not bear to see all the Law disappear.}}

